\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Remark}
\title{How the divergence enters alignment objectives}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{rlhf}
\tag{dpo}

\p{The KL-regularized reward objective appears as equation (3) in Section 3
of \citek{rafailov2023direct}. Behavior-policy ratios, clipped ratios, and
KL penalties enter alignment objectives for different purposes.}

\p{A coefficient multiplying #{D_{\mathrm{KL}}} declares an optimization
tradeoff. It is neither a guarantee that every sampled ratio is small nor an
independent evaluation of the resulting policy.}
